    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. looks doable. i'm a bit worried about the fatigue though, especially since i work a desk job and i'm usually pretty tired by the time i get to the gym. how do i handle those days where i feel like i just don't have the energy to hit my numbers? should i just push through it or what?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not push through extreme fatigue when your primary goal is steady strength gain, as it can lead to poor form and injury risks. Instead, switch to a \"maintenance\" week that same day where you perform 50-70% of your usual weight or simply drop to accessory movements like lunges or rows. For many desk workers, fighting through exhaustion is counterproductive, so listening to your body to preserve long-term consistency is often the smarter strategic choice.",
      "source": "target",
